{"sessionId": "aaaaaaaa-bbbb-4ccc-8ddd-eeeeeeeeeeee", "cwd": "/home/dev/acme-app", "gitBranch": "main", "version": "2.1.303", "entrypoint": "cli", "isSidechain": false, "type": "assistant", "uuid": "a1", "parentUuid": "u1", "timestamp": "2026-10-20T10:00:05Z", "message": {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "For a single-writer orderbook on one machine, SQLite is enough and removes a server to run. Postgres pays off once several services write at once."}]}}
